AgentHawk Core is defensive, dual-use security software.

It parses npm dependency requests, normalizes bounded public registry and OSV evidence, and applies deterministic repository policy before a dependency is admitted. Its intended use is to help developers and coding agents identify risk signals and require explicit review.

The package does not install or execute inspected package code, exploit systems, collect credentials, or claim that a dependency is benign. Security findings remain limited by the enabled evidence sources and policy.
